From 4d5a05f0b3aebabb8066e13524415773ee7cb87e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Paul Lamb <paul@paulscode.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 19:00:15 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/7] bolt12: port the BOLT 12 codecs from LND master

LND v0.21.3-beta has onion messages, blinded-path invoices and the RPCs
to send and receive onion messages, but no BOLT 12 codecs; those exist
only on master (0.22-dev) as the bolt12 package. This brings that
package in at master 606321b, byte-identical except for the two
import paths of btcd's split modules (chaincfg/v2 and chainhash/v2,
which this tree has as one module), with the lnwire pieces it depends
on: the blinded-path TLV records, the introduction-node type, the
bounds helper, master's pure-TLV helpers with a per-protocol signed
range, and the AddOpt and SetOptFromMap optional-record helpers. All
of it is verbatim from master; the package's own tests and the BOLT 12
spec vectors pass here.

The package is left unmodified on purpose, so it can follow master.
Its read validators take the active chain explicitly, and its default
of Bitcoin mainnet for an absent chain is the spec's meaning: an offer
or request that names no chain is for Bitcoin, and the offers layer
above this refuses it by passing the BLAKE2b chain hash.

(cherry picked from commit fd72f08619515082a10745ceb9602fb9f0ae6e5c)
